WEBVTT

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.540
I have become one with speed.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.460
Then,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.310
your goal is to have Sergey beat Jack, 
so you can take control of City?

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:37.930
True order can only be created 
by those with power.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.280
No.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.610
D-Wheels.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.790
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.450
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.960
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.060
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.010
Soul Fist

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.750
My turn!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.220
Sergey got an Action Card!

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.250
At the same time, the effect of Field Spell 
Earthbound Tundra activates.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.960
The Action Card I picked up is banished,

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.120
300 damage is dealt to you,

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.170
and the attack points of one of your 
monsters is reduced by 300.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.200
Sergey gets another Action Card!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.810
Jack takes another hit of damage!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.150
After taking a series of hits, 
your expression remains unchanged?

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:25.780
Boring!

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.360
S-Sergey has begun destroying the course!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:31.790
Hang on a minute...

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.930
We need to use that later!

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.390
J-Jack...

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.400
Stop it! That's cheating!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.620
Is Jack being driven back?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.870
Sergey's beating the king?

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.120
There's another Action Card, just ahead.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.850
Jack's in danger of taking more damage!

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.380
Great job! Jack uses the wall for a big jump!

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.660
Looks like you're standing still.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.010
Oh, no!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.560
We thought he might come back, 
but he was knocked away!

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.460
For a third time, Earthbound Tundra's 
effect deals Jack damage!

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.400
Monster...

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.110
H-He was knocked away? Jack's jump...

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.600
It seems getting ahead of him is impossible.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.420
At this rate, he'll just keep 
shaving down Jack's life.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:31.780
What?

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.580
That's right.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.230
Your hope is showing cracks,

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.850
tragically turning to despair.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.550
What will you accomplish, driving the 
people of City to despair?

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.210
A new hope.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.170
A new hope?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.140
In the form of Jean-Michel Roget.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.680
I activate my spell card Earthbound 
Rescue from my hand!

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.960
I add one Earthbound monster and one spell 
card, from my graveyard to my hand.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.270
And because a Field Spell is active,

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.630
I can Special Summon Stone 
Sweeper from my hand!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:27.340
I also summon my Tuner Monster 
Earthbound Prisoner Ground Keeper.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.370
I activate my spell card Harmonic Synchro Fusion!

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.530
I use two monsters on my side of the field

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.420
as components for a Synchro and Fusion Summon.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.540
Your simultaneous Synchro 
and Fusion Summons...

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.890
It's become a tired, old trick.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:48.860
Level 1 Ground Keeper tunes 
Level 5 Stone Sweeper!

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.470
Fairy that dwells in the ground,

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.700
use your bewitching power to shake all creation!

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.770
Synchro Summon!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:05.040
Appear, Level 6 Earthbound 
Servant Geo Gremlin!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.960
And I fuse Stone Sweeper and Ground Keeper!

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.670
One trapped in stone,

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:16.520
join with one sealed in earth, 
and take hold of the ground.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.990
Fusion Summon!

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.350
Appear, Level 6 Earthbound 
Servant Geo Gremlina!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.290
King,

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.900
it's time to suffer.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.870
Suffer, you say?

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.340
I activate Geo Gremlin's effect.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:35.340
Now, Jack Atlas,

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:42.700
you must decide whether Scarlight Red 
Dragon Archfiend is destroyed or not.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:45.020
If it's destroyed,

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.260
you can skip this turn's Battle Phase,

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.410
and you'll be given a one-turn stay of defeat.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.200
If it's not destroyed,

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:58.060
I recover life, equal to Scarlight Red 
Dragon Archfiend's attack points.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:03.560
And my monsters will fall upon the 
weakened Red Dragon.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.890
And, King, you will lose!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.040
Now, choose.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.350
Not much of a choice.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:17.290
Jack would never destroy Red Dragon!

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.420
But if he doesn't destroy it, he'll lose!

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.490
To see him cornered to this degree...

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.960
He has no choice but to destroy it.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.820
Yes, the best decision now is to destroy it.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:31.560
To preserve hope for later.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.100
But that hope will be immediately 
crushed, as well.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.120
When Red Dragon is destroyed, 
Gremlina's effect will activate.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.040
Gremlina's effect?

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:47.770
When an opponent's monster 
is destroyed by an effect,

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.800
Geo Gremlina destroys all monsters on its field,

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.290
dealing the sum of their attack points as damage.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.690
The sum of Gremlin and Gremlina's 
attack points are 4000.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.910
Jack has 2500 life remaining.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:03.960
Then, it's...

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.850
Checkmate.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.900
King! Time to make your choice.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.770
There is no choice.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.870
So you choose destruction?

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.290
Fool...

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:19.120
You think I'd throw away my soul, 
just because you challenge me?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.510
Soul?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.320
Red Dragon is the proof of my soul!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.490
No matter how difficult the situation, 
I would never destroy it!

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.720
Not even if it means my death!

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:31.920
What?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.060
Impossible!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.000
Jack chooses not to destroy it, 
and Sergey recovers 1500 life!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.550
Then, shatter, along with your soul.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:50.960
Battle! Geo Gremlin attacks Scarlight 
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.910
If Red Dragon is destroyed, that's 500 damage!

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:58.160
After Geo Gremlina makes its direct attack,

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.290
Jack, with only 2000 life points, will lose.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.350
Jack!

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.340
After all that, quite a pitiful end.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.590
But it is time for King to leave the stage.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:13.060
Die in humiliation, Jack Atlas!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.740
Then, shatter, along with your soul.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:29.280
Battle! Geo Gremlin attacks Scarlight 
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:33.150
Die in humiliation, Jack Atlas!

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.430
I activate my trap Red Gem.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.230
This turn, one Red monster cannot be destroyed!

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.680
But you still take damage.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:52.180
And Geo Gremlina attacks Red Dragon!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.240
Red Gem's activation prevents 
Red Dragon's destruction!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.610
Damn you... You'll protect 
Red Dragon to the end?

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.240
I told you,

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.220
Red Dragon symbolizes Jack Atlas's duel.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.560
It is my soul!

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.260
To burn one's soul to its limit, and seize 
victory amidst its light...

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.100
To burn with the heat of the blazing sun...

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.740
To shine with the radiance of stars in space...

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.700
That is how I...

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.170
How the king duels!

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:36.440
What's wrong?

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.800
I end my turn.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:48.390
My turn!

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.480
Nonsense! Soul isn't enough to win a duel.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.660
Behold what I am!

00:10:55.660 --> 00:11:00.670
The perfect body and perfect 
tactics, woven together!

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:03.780
You are a buffoon.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:10.190
There are seven Action Cards ahead of me.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.890
You're finished, King!

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:19.620
Stop... Any more of this will be 
too much for you to take!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:26.500
Jack sees Sergey's momentary drop 
in speed, and closes the distance!

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.630
How long will the fool prattle on?

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.600
Damn you...

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.070
Begone, King!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.270
There is no such thing as perfection.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.030
If there is, it is but one thing.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.780
That is I!

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.020
Jack quickly closes in on Sergey.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.990
It's a slipstream!

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.990
But you still won't get ahead of me.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:53.960
What will you do?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.930
A moment's light is enough.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.260
Light?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:04.200
Even if it is but a faint, momentary light, 
it will illuminate the path to victory.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.800
That is how I... How the king duels!

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:13.790
That's right! This is our king, Jack Atlas!

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.210
It's time for him to really show his stuff!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.450
The rioting has... stopped?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.890
There's an Action Card ahead!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:28.360
Let's begin the countdown to your defeat!

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.010
What?

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:49.250
Jack exploited a momentary opening 
to grab an Action Card!

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.040
Earthbound Tundra's effect.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:57.690
When you pick up an Action Card, it sends 
my Action Card to the graveyard.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:02.290
Now, you can't deal damage with 
Earthbound Tundra's effect!

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.440
Jack... Magnificent.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.500
He's negated the threat from 
Sergey's Earthbound Tundra!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.170
And there's an Action Card 
right in front of Jack!

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:13.640
He ignored it?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.360
What?

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:17.770
Jack didn't take the Action Card? 
What's his angle?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.850
Now, you will witness the king's true duel!

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:28.160
The fool... If Sergey gets an Action Card now,

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.490
he will seize the initiative with 
Earthbound Tundra once more.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.960
Sergey goes for the Action Card... 
And he ignores it, too?!

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.130
What is going on?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.420
I'll defeat you, Jack Atlas!

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.300
With all the power I have! Beautifully!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:50.520
Good to hear it! Then, keeping Red 
Dragon safe was worthwhile!

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:58.820
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:01.050
My turn!

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:05.980
Battle! Geo Gremlin attacks Red Dragon!

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.440
I activate Action Spell Tenacity.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.920
When there is one monster 
on my side of the field,

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.370
that monster cannot be destroyed 
by battle this turn!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.570
But you still take damage.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:24.890
Now, Geo Gremlina attacks Red Dragon!

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.250
Tenacity prevents its destruction!

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.260
Jack prevents his monster's destruction, 
but consecutive hits reduce his life!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.400
That's right... Crush him!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:41.680
Teach him that in the face of absolute 
power, hope is meaningless!

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:46.700
Then, the foolish citizens, learning of 
my great power, will bow.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:50.620
And my domination will begin...

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.940
My ideal world—

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.170
Your ideal will never become reality.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:58.180
What?

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:03.380
A world where you have to use force 
to get your way means nothing.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:07.620
Then, pray tell, what kind of 
world does have meaning?

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:09.090
One of smiles.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.060
Smiles?

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.400
A world where anyone can smile.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:16.290
That's an ideal world, a world with meaning!

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:18.320
Nonsense...

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.770
Smiles bring people together. 
They let them communicate.

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:25.860
Hearts that communicate...

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:30.340
They won't be broken by control 
that's exerted through power.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.430
Dueling is the same way.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:34.710
Power alone won't resonate with the heart!

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.010
Resonate with the heart? A duel?

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:39.450
Ridiculous.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.980
I activate my spell Earthbound Fusion.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.860
When a Field Spell is active, I can 
perform Fusion Summons.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:51.660
I fuse Geo Gremlin and Geo Gremlina!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.810
Demon that governs the earth,

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.670
demon that takes hold of the ground...

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:03.410
Let both sexes combine, and come to 
us from the great earth's depths!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.440
Fusion Summon!

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:12.150
Appear, Level 10 Earthbound 
Servant Geo Grasha!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:14.590
3000 attack points?

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:15.820
Battle.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:19.590
Geo Grasha attacks Red Dragon!

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:21.800
And its effect activates.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.120
When it battles a Synchro or Fusion Monster,

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:27.530
it renders that monster's attack points 0!

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.210
Even preventing its destruction 
with Tenacity won't save you!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.820
Darkness Miasma!

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.640
Is Jack done for this time?

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.350
I activate the effect of Red Mirror in my hand.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.310
When one of your monsters attacks,

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:50.020
I can send this card to the graveyard, to 
return one Red monster from it to my hand.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:54.260
I add Red Warg, then send it and 
Dark Resonator to my graveyard,

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.230
to activate my trap card Red Soul!

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:00.360
This turn, Red Dragon isn't destroyed,

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:04.900
and damage is reduced by the total attack points 
of the monsters sent to the graveyard!

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:06.510
Meaningless struggles.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:11.080
Jack reduces the damage by 2700.

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:14.810
He holds on with a mere 200 life!

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.330
The road Sergey destroyed is collapsing.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.760
Sergey's falling!

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:31.830
King uses Red Dragon to save 
Sergey from falling!

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.910
The duel must be finished as a duel.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.800
That is how I do things.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.540
Beau...

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:47.990
Beautiful...

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.270
Yuya, I'm so moved right now!

00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.890
Looking good, Jack!

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:01.900
Go, Jack!

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:04.100
You're the Commons' star of hope!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.280
Jack, you're incredible!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.070
You're our hope!

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:11.210
Jack barely manages to save Sergey,

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:15.040
but now that he's in back, the danger 
from Earthbound Tundra is renewed.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.510
And there's an Action Card right ahead!

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:20.120
Sergey! Take the Action Card!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.250
Crush King with Earthbound Tundra!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:25.220
Sergey goes for the Action Card...

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.420
And ignores it!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.390
Sergey!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:30.890
Beautiful!

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:34.630
King, this duel is absolutely beautiful.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:39.360
Let's decorate our duel, make it 
even more beautiful!

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.330
I end my turn!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.030
Very well.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:45.630
You damned fool!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:48.580
Their hearts reached each other.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.710
Sergey, take the Action Card! Sergey!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:57.920
It's no use. No amount of power 
can control those two now.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.350
Bring it, King!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:08.680
Can you hear it? The pulse of my soul?

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.830
The cry of my soul, as it burns its brightest?

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:14.200
It's my...

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.500
My turn!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.910
It's here, the card on which 
my soul is inscribed.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.610
I activate my Equip Spell Soul Fist.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.390
Let it be carved on your soul!

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:33.020
I equip it to Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:38.650
Until my End Phase, Soul Fist 
changes the attack points

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:43.790
of one monster, with more points 
than it has, to equal its points!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:49.270
Wow! Geo Grasha, who turned 
Red Dragon's attack points to 0,

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:52.470
now has its own attack points changed to 0!

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.800
Then, I activate Red Dragon's effect.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:58.810
Once per turn, it can destroy all 
Special Summoned monsters

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:01.450
with attack points equal to, 
or less than, its own,

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:05.510
dealing 500 damage to you for each.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:08.420
Absolute Power Flame!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:21.520
Geo Grasha's destruction activates 
Soul Fist's other effect.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:23.030
Until the end of this turn,

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:28.970
the equipped monster's attack points equal the 
destroyed monster's original attack points!

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:37.500
B-Beautiful...

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.250
Our hope!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.190
King's soul!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.200
Scarlight Red Demon...

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.660
...Archfiend!

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:52.960
Battle.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:59.200
Your soul... I see now why
 you didn't destroy it.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:03.910
Scarlight Red Demon Archfiend 
attacks directly.

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:07.520
Red Hot Crimson Hell Burning!

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:18.260
Red Dragon!

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:25.030
Don't interrupt my beautiful fall!

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:28.090
So long, King.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.290
Sergey Volkov...

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.110
Beautiful!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.440
The winner is my... our...

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:44.420
City's Jack Atlas!

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:58.560
I-I-Impossible!

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:13.450
Jack! Jack! Jack! Jack!

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:53.710
I, Jean-Michel Roget, 
hereby declare martial law.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:54.950
Martial law?

00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:58.980
Don't be fooled! Roget isn't 
trying to restore order.

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:01.850
He's trying to take over City!

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:06.160
Jack wants Yuya Sakaki to show 
him the duel he believes in.

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:09.630
If you're trying to accomplish something...

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:10.940
Do not falter!

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:15.360
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Duel You Believe In.

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:17.260
The fun is only getting started!
